<div class="qul-docs">
  <h2>About stem data</h2>

  <p>
    The <strong>stem</strong> of a word is the word itself with the pieces attached to it taken off. Arabic
    joins several small words onto the front and back of a word, so one written word such as
    <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">فَأَزَلَّهُمَا</span> ("so he made the two of them slip") holds a particle, a verb and a pronoun. Its
    stem is just the verb, <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">أَزَلَّ</span>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every word of the Quran has exactly one stem. Words that share a stem are the same word with different
    pieces attached, so stems are useful for search and for finding every place a word is used.
  </p>

  <h3>The article</h3>
  <p>The definite article <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ال</span> ("the") is removed.</p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="[&_td]:align-middle">
      <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Word</th>
        <th>Location</th>
        <th>Stem</th>
        <th>Removed</th>
      </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">ٱلۡحَمۡدُ</span></td>
        <td><code>1:2:1</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">حَمْدُ</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ال</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ</span></td>
        <td><code>1:1:3</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">رَّحْمَٰنِ</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ال</span></td>
      </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>Prefixes: joined particles</h3>
  <p>
    One-letter particles written as part of the next word are removed: <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">وَ</span> and <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">فَ</span> ("and",
    "so"), the prepositions <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">بِ</span> ("with, in") and <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">لِ</span> ("for, to"), and the <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">يَا</span> used to call
    someone ("O").
  </p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="[&_td]:align-middle">
      <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Word</th>
        <th>Location</th>
        <th>Stem</th>
        <th>Removed</th>
      </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">وَبَشِّرِ</span></td>
        <td><code>2:25:1</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">بَشِّرِ</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">وَ</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">فَأَخۡرَجَ</span></td>
        <td><code>2:22:12</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">أَخْرَجَ</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">فَ</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">بِمَآ</span></td>
        <td><code>2:4:3</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">مَآ</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">بِ</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">لِلرَّحۡمَٰنِ</span></td>
        <td><code>19:26:13</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">رَّحْمَٰنِ</span></td>
        <td dir="ltr"><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">لِ</span> + <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ال</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">يَٰٓأَيُّهَا</span></td>
        <td><code>4:1:1</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">أَيُّهَا</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">يَا</span></td>
      </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>Suffixes: attached pronouns</h3>
  <p>
    Pronouns joined to the end of a noun, preposition or verb, such as <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـهِ</span> ("him"), <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـهِمۡ</span>
    ("them") and <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـنَا</span> ("us"), are removed.
  </p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="[&_td]:align-middle">
      <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Word</th>
        <th>Location</th>
        <th>Stem</th>
        <th>Removed</th>
      </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">عَلَيۡهِ</span></td>
        <td><code>2:37:7</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">عَلَيْ</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـهِ</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">رَّبِّهِمۡ</span></td>
        <td><code>2:5:5</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">رَّبِّ</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـهِمۡ</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">أَيۡدِيهِمۡ</span></td>
        <td><code>2:255:30</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">أَيْدِي</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـهِمۡ</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">ٱهۡدِنَا</span></td>
        <td><code>1:6:1</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">اهْدِ</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـنَا</span></td>
      </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>Suffixes: verb endings</h3>
  <p>
    The endings that say who did the action, such as <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـتَ</span> ("you") and <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـُواْ</span> ("they"), are
    removed too, along with any pronoun after them.
  </p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="[&_td]:align-middle">
      <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Word</th>
        <th>Location</th>
        <th>Stem</th>
        <th>Removed</th>
      </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">أَنۡعَمۡتَ</span></td>
        <td><code>1:7:3</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">أَنْعَمْ</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـتَ</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">ءَامَنُواْ</span></td>
        <td><code>2:9:4</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">ءَامَنُ</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـُواْ</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ</span></td>
        <td><code>2:3:7</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">رَزَقْ</span></td>
        <td dir="ltr"><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـنَا</span> + <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـهُمۡ</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">فَيَعۡلَمُونَ</span></td>
        <td><code>2:26:15</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">يَعْلَمُ</span></td>
        <td dir="ltr"><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">فَ</span> + <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـُونَ</span></td>
      </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>What stays</h3>
  <p>Everything that belongs to the word itself is kept, including:</p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="[&_td]:align-middle">
      <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Word</th>
        <th>Location</th>
        <th>Stem</th>
        <th>Kept</th>
      </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">نَعۡبُدُ</span></td>
        <td><code>1:5:2</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">نَعْبُدُ</span></td>
        <td>The present-tense prefix <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">نَ</span> ("we")</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">جَمِيعٗا</span></td>
        <td><code>3:103:4</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">جَمِيعًا</span></td>
        <td>The case ending</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">أُحِلَّتۡ</span></td>
        <td><code>5:1:6</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">أُحِلَّتْ</span></td>
        <td>The feminine <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ـتْ</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">ٱللَّهُ</span></td>
        <td><code>2:7:2</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">اللَّهُ</span></td>
        <td>The article in the name of Allah</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">وَإِيَّاكَ</span></td>
        <td><code>1:5:3</code></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic" dir="rtl">إِيَّاكَ</span></td>
        <td><span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">إِيَّاكَ</span> is itself a pronoun, so only <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">وَ</span> goes</td>
      </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>


