  <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-info">
    <strong>ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ</strong> and <strong>ٱلرَّحۡمَةَ</strong> share a root but not a stem: they are different
    words. Use roots to group words by meaning, lemmas to group them by dictionary entry, and stems to find
    one word in all its attached forms.
  </div>

  <h2>SQLite format</h2>
  <p>
    The download is a SQLite database with two tables: <code>stems</code> (12,113 rows, one per stem) and
    <code>stem_words</code> (one row per word of the Quran, linking it to its stem).
  </p>

  <h3>Table: <code>stems</code></h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Column</th>
      <th>Type</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>id</code></td>
      <td>INTEGER</td>
      <td>Stem id, used by <code>stem_words.stem_id</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>text</code></td>
      <td>TEXT</td>
      <td>Stem with full diacritics</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>text_clean</code></td>
      <td>TEXT</td>
      <td>Stem without diacritics, for search</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>words_count</code></td>
      <td>INTEGER</td>
      <td>How many words in the Quran have this stem</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>uniq_words_count</code></td>
      <td>INTEGER</td>
      <td>How many different forms those words take</td>
    </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="docs-code">
    <div class="docs-code-header"><span>Sample rows</span></div>
    <pre><code>id    | text        | text_clean | words_count | uniq_words_count
368   | حَمْدُ       | حمد        | 28          | 2
6475  | رَّحْمَٰنِ    | رحمان      | 33          | 3
10329 | رَّحِيمِ      | رحيم       | 6           | 1</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p>
    For example, the stem <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">رَّحْمَٰنِ</span> appears 33 times in 3 forms:
    <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ</span>, <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">لِلرَّحۡمَٰنِ</span>
    and <span class="me-quran docs-arabic-inline" dir="rtl">بِٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ</span>.
  </p>

  <h3>Table: <code>stem_words</code></h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Column</th>
      <th>Type</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>stem_id</code></td>
      <td>INTEGER</td>
      <td>The word's stem, from <code>stems.id</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>word_location</code></td>
      <td>TEXT</td>
      <td>Word position as <code>surah:ayah:word</code>, e.g. <code>1:1:3</code> is the third word of the first ayah</td>
    </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="docs-code">
    <div class="docs-code-header"><span>Sample rows</span></div>
    <pre><code>stem_id | word_location
368     | 1:2:1
6475    | 1:1:3
6475    | 1:3:1
10329   | 1:1:4</code></pre>
  </div>

  <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-info">
    Rows are not stored in Quran order. When you need them in reading order, sort by surah, ayah and word
    number rather than by the <code>word_location</code> text.
  </div>

  <h2>Example queries</h2>

  <h3>Find the stem of a word</h3>
  <div class="docs-code">
    <div class="docs-code-header">
      <span>SQL</span>
      <button type="button" class="docs-copy-btn" data-action="docs-copy#copy">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>SELECT stems.*
FROM stem_words
JOIN stems ON stems.id = stem_words.stem_id
WHERE stem_words.word_location = '1:1:3';</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h3>Every place a stem is used</h3>
  <div class="docs-code">
    <div class="docs-code-header">
      <span>SQL</span>
      <button type="button" class="docs-copy-btn" data-action="docs-copy#copy">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>SELECT word_location
FROM stem_words
WHERE stem_id = 6475;  -- رَّحْمَٰنِ: 33 locations</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h3>Search by stem without diacritics</h3>
  <div class="docs-code">
    <div class="docs-code-header">
      <span>SQL</span>
      <button type="button" class="docs-copy-btn" data-action="docs-copy#copy">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>SELECT id, text, words_count
FROM stems
WHERE text_clean = 'حمد';
-- 368  | حَمْدُ | 28
-- 1422 | حَمْدِ | 15</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h3>Most used stems</h3>
  <div class="docs-code">
    <div class="docs-code-header">
      <span>SQL</span>
      <button type="button" class="docs-copy-btn" data-action="docs-copy#copy">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>SELECT text, words_count, uniq_words_count
FROM stems
ORDER BY words_count DESC
LIMIT 10;</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>
